06:10.110 --> 06:14.610
of exclamation points like that and a bunch up here.

06:14.610 --> 06:17.280
Okay, so now I'm gonna add and commit my changes

06:17.280 --> 06:21.960
on master git add dot, git commit dash M, you know,

06:21.960 --> 06:24.033
update hello greeting.

06:25.260 --> 06:28.293
Now I'm gonna switch back to our goodbye branch.

06:29.820 --> 06:31.590
So at the moment, goodbye,

06:31.590 --> 06:34.680
this Goodbye branch still has the older version, right?

06:34.680 --> 06:36.390
We don't have all these exclamation points.

06:36.390 --> 06:39.810
And if I update this to be goodbye world

06:39.810 --> 06:41.920
and this says goodbye here

06:43.800 --> 06:46.770
but I don't add and commit, I switch over to master

06:46.770 --> 06:49.980
from here. I have unstaged uncommitted changes.

06:49.980 --> 06:54.090
I'm gonna switch back to master, it won't let me.

06:54.090 --> 06:56.700
This is that second scenario, your local changes

06:56.700 --> 06:59.040
to the following files would be overwritten

06:59.040 --> 07:02.640
by switching, or by checkout, index.html.

07:02.640 --> 07:04.110
Please commit your changes

07:04.110 --> 07:06.510
or stash them before you switch branches.

07:06.510 --> 07:08.370
So this is a common scenario

07:08.370 --> 07:11.160
at least somewhat common where I need to switch over

07:11.160 --> 07:13.770
I need to go back to this master branch for whatever reason.

07:13.770 --> 07:16.260
Imagine it's a much more complicated project.

07:16.260 --> 07:17.760
I need to switch over to some branch.

07:17.760 --> 07:19.110
It doesn't have to be master

07:19.110 --> 07:21.930
but I have work that is uncommitted

07:21.930 --> 07:24.788
on my current branch and git is not gonna let me switch

07:24.788 --> 07:27.690
or I don't want the changes to come with me.

07:27.690 --> 07:29.640
Like I didn't want those purple changes to come

07:29.640 --> 07:31.156
